author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.6, 4.7 master\nTested in 4.5 too and had a similar but different bug\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev (0b423c83b) - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9579) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nSSR in VR has a sort of inverted depth effect right now, it looks like reflections are bulging out at you\nTo my eyes it looks like it could be the reflections from the right eye are being displayed in the left eye and vise-versa?\n\n<img width=\"1928\" height=\"1013\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/182da207-85f9-4508-9c34-9e025511bc64\" />\n\n(Ignore the playspace warning lol) It should be easy to see in the screenshot how the reflections lean strangely\n\nThe result is the same in D3D and Vulkan\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Get a reflective surface\n2. Turn on SSR\n3. View the surface reflections in VR\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[vr_screenspace_reflection_mrp_2026-04-16_03-42-48.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26781619/vr_screenspace_reflection_mrp_2026-04-16_03-42-48.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"htt